  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. That is, the Startup page's \\\"Launch at login\\\" toggle is disabled by the OS setting but shows no reason, which is a regression from PR #20200. Two older tickets are related but don't match. terminal#6254 is an old request to show UX for the different StartupTaskState values, mainly DisabledByUser. terminal#12564 is about backing the setting with the OS startup state. For now, check Windows Settings > Apps > Startup and re-enable Terminal there. That should let you toggle the setting again. The ticket should stay open as a new bug. The localized reason text already exists, so the fix is probably to hook it back up in the Startup page.\"}",
